{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L173-L186","doc":"**`T_w⁻¹` lies in length `≤ ℓ(w)`** — the Bruhat-free half of the triangularity that\nMathas' 3.9 needs, and the half that the probe measured at 32/32.\n\nWhat this does **not** say is the Bruhat half: that the support sits inside `[e, w⁻¹]`.\nThat is measured, not proved, and proving it needs a subword order the corpus does not\nhave. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv_mul_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv_mul_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L170-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.Tw_mul_TwInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.Tw_mul_TwInv","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L167-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInv","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L163-L165","doc":"**`T_w⁻¹`**, built from the chosen reduced word for `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L152-L159","doc":"**The length bound, along a word.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_mul_TwOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_mul_TwOf","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L144-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwOf_mul_TwInvOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwOf_mul_TwInvOf","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L134-L142","doc":"**`TwInvOf` is the inverse of `TwOf`** — the check that the `foldr` ordering is the\nright one.  A `foldl` here would not be an inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwOf_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwOf_cons","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L128-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.foldl_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.foldl_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L118-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_cons","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L114-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf_nil","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.TwInvOf","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L108-L110","doc":"`T_ω⁻¹` along a word: `σ_{i_1}⁻¹ ⋯ σ_{i_k}⁻¹`, the reverse order of `TwOf`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.σInv_mul_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.σInv_mul_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L95-L104","doc":"The same for `σᵢ⁻¹`, which is `⅟q · (σᵢ − (q−1))` and so adds no new support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.σ_mul_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.σ_mul_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L70-L91","doc":"**The filtration step.**  Multiplying by a generator raises length by at most one,\nbecause `σ_mul_Tw` lands in the span of `T_v` and `T_{v·sᵢ}` in both of its branches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.length_mul_sw_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.length_mul_sw_le","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L64-L68","doc":"`ℓ(v · sᵢ) ≤ ℓ(v) + 1` — either branch of `length_mul_simple`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.spanLe_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.spanLe_mono","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L58-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.one_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.one_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L54-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.Tw_mem_spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.Tw_mem_spanLe","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.spanLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TwInverseLength.spanLe","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TwInverseLength.lean#L45-L48","doc":"**`span {T_v : ℓ(v) ≤ k}`** — the length filtration of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}